# Privacy posture: DEFAULT-DENY. The viewer is server-free; users load their own
# .threads at view time. Public hosting of any real-conversation artifact is
# possession-is-capability, so an artifact is public the moment it ships under a
# known path. We therefore ignore ALL .threads and explicitly re-allow ONLY the
# files we intend to be reachable on threads.adityaarpitha.com.
#
# (The root .gitignore's `lct_app/public/*.threads` rule is NOT applied when
#  Vercel deploys from this subdirectory, so the policy must live here.)
#
# To share a new map: drop it in public/ under an UNGUESSABLE filename
# (corpus-<random>.threads — the random suffix is the "key", Notion-style) and
# add a matching `!public/<name>` line below. Never re-allow a guessable name.

public/*.threads

# Vercel rebuilds the bundle itself, so never upload the local build output —
# Vite copies EVERY public/*.threads into dist/, which would otherwise sneak the
# gitignored real-conversation artifacts past the public/ rule above.
dist/

# --- deliberately public (obscure filenames act as the share key) ---
!public/m17-db6a940c.threads
!public/corpus-81b50f062006c764.threads
!public/call-2026-05-23-30fbdd9d854e7058.threads
